{{#markdown }}
### Overview

Add lazyLoad to plugin setup:
```javascript
lazyLoad: true
```
LazyLoad HTML structure requires `class="owl-lazy"` and `data-src="url_to_img"` or/and `data-src-retina="url_to_highres_img"`.
If you set above settings not on `<img>` but on other DOM element then Owl will load an image into css inline background style.
You can even use picture tags with different sources by adding the `owl-lazy` class to the source tag and a data-srcset attribute.

### Setup
```javascript
$('.owl-carousel').owlCarousel({
	items:1,
	lazyLoad:true,
	lazyLoadEager:1,
	loop:true,
	margin:10,
	autoHeight:true
});
```
### Option

If you want to preload images you can also add the option ```lazyLoadEager``` to the settings object, where the value
indicates how many items to the right (and left, when loop is ```true```) will be pre-loaded.

### HTML:

```html
<div class="owl-carousel owl-theme">
	<img class="owl-lazy" data-src="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-1.png" data-src-retina="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-1.png" alt="Lazy-loaded item 1">
	<img class="owl-lazy" data-src="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-2.png" data-src-retina="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-2.png" alt="Lazy-loaded item 2">
  <picture>
      <source class="owl-lazy" media="(min-width: 650px)" data-srcset="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-3.png">
      <source class="owl-lazy" media="(min-width: 350px)" data-srcset="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-3.png">
      <img class="owl-lazy" data-src="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-3.png" alt="Lazy-loaded item 3">
  </picture>
	<img class="owl-lazy" data-src="{{assets}}/img/lazyload-block-4.png" alt="Lazy-loaded item 4">
</div>
```
{{/markdown }}
<script>
jQuery(document).ready(function($) {
	$('.owl-carousel').owlCarousel({
		items:1,
		lazyLoad:true,
    lazyLoadEager: 1,
		loop:true,
		margin:10,
    autoHeight: true
	});
});
</script>
